<title>COSTA RICA: Panama pushes for Central America free trade pact.</title>
<headline>Panama pushes for Central America free trade pact.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Costa Rica 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama's Foreign Affairs Minister Ricardo Arias said on Tuesday that Panama has readied a proposal for a free trade pact with the rest of the nations in Central America.</p>
<p>Speaking at a press conference in the Costa Rican capital, Arias said Panama wanted to strengthen commercial relations with Guatemala, El Salvador, Honduras, Nicaragua and Costa Rica.</p>
<p>&quot;The proposal is being evaluated at this time by the Ministry of Central American Economic Integration to be later presented to the governments in the region,&quot; Arias said.</p>
<p>((--Costa Rica bureau, +506 224-2949))</p>
</text>
